    "notes": "Headed Chrome on real Radeon hardware, with state sampled each RAF. CPU throttling is a separate CDP stress case and leaves the GPU enabled. Each warm pass uses 44 simulated seconds with straight boost, two bank reversals, climb and dive. The cold pass moves to an unseen neighborhood and resumes as soon as the current collision ring is ready. Inputs are scheduled by simulation time at animation frame boundaries, so nominal trajectories match with small frame-quantization differences.",
